<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto IV, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1175–<a href="/years/1218">1218</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Otto of Brunswick</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto IV, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-welf">Welf dynasty</a>, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> from 1198 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> from 1209. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a> and nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a>, he fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Staufer</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-of-swabia">Philip of Swabia</a> for the crown and later broke with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iii">Pope Innocent III</a>. His defeat with his English and Flemish allies at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bouvines">Battle of Bouvines</a> in 1214 ended his power, and Frederick II replaced him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-iv-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Otto IV, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="332" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Otto Posse (1847-1921) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ottta4Brunsvicky.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
